  #line-at(70.944pt, 173.78pt, "Gas sensors based on layered TMDCs (transition-metal dichalcogenides) such as MoS")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(453.22pt, 174.74pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(456.7pt, 173.78pt, " have attracted ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 187.22pt, "considerable attention recently and are considered as a promising alternative to the conventional ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 200.66pt, "metal-oxide-based gas sensing devices. Recent studies on TMDC gas sensors have mainly addressed ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 213.98pt, "either the theoretical description of adsorption mechanisms or the fabrication of test devices and the ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 227.42pt, "investigation of their gas sensing performance. However, a suitable approach for modeling the gas ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 240.86pt, "sensing behavior of TMDC devices and for establishing a reliable connection between theoretical ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 254.3pt, "results and the response of experimental devices when exposed to gases remains absent. To bridge ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 267.77pt, "this gap, in the present work a new Langmuir-based adsorption model, capable of calculating both the ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 281.21pt, "sensor sensitivity and selectivity, is developed and applied to MoS")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(364.39pt, 282.17pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(367.87pt, 281.21pt, "-based gas sensors. It is shown that ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 294.65pt, "by using appropriate published data for the adsorption energy and the charge transfer as input data, ")
  #line-at(70.944pt, 308.09pt, "the reported experimental sensitivities of MoS")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(278.81pt, 309.05pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(282.29pt, 308.09pt, " gas sensors can be well reproduced by the model.   ")
